{"uid":"b0f1dab1ae40d37b","name":"test_harness_decision_wins_over_a_disagreeing_worker_payload_claim","fullName":"tests.test_worker_harness_owned_status#test_harness_decision_wins_over_a_disagreeing_worker_payload_claim","historyId":"1393656ff7203cf4f45e46c59163ac4d","time":{"start":1791980793310,"stop":1791980793589,"duration":279},"description":"The scheduler assigns \"001\" (first in list order, no priority/deps).\n    The fake agent's payload instead claims completion of \"002\" -- a task\n    it was never assigned. Task 116's ORIGINAL claim, pinned here before\n    v0.13 task 006 (#92 site 4)'s cutover, was: `outcome == (\"tail\",)` and\n    `sup._abort_reason` mentioning \"contract violation\" -- a single\n    disagreeing claim was fatal on the FIRST offence, with no re-ask and no\n    ladder at all.\n\n    The NEW claim keeps the old one's real content -- the move is STILL\n    refused, and the record that actually persists is the harness's OWN\n    decision: \"001\" sits exactly where the harness itself put it\n    (`in-progress`, claimed before spawn), \"002\" is untouched (still\n    `pending`) -- and adds what the old assertion could not see: the\n    disagreement is carried back to the SAME worker verbatim on every\n    re-ask through `contract_enforcement.enforce_contract` (the EXACT SAME\n    ladder `_step_generic_hat`'s sites 1/2 and worker's own site 3 already\n    use), the ladder runs the FULL `contract_retry_max + 1` attempts each\n    pass (never fewer, never more), and an exhausted ladder is an\n    agent-fault continuation -- never an abort, no `_abort_reason`, no\n    \"contract violation\" log message. Because the disagreement never\n    resolves, tasks.json never moves on any pass, so it takes exactly one\n    pass to record every task's fresh `criteriaFingerprint` baseline (task\n    008's own first-sight bookkeeping, itself \"progress\" for the\n    stagnation counter even though nothing about the disagreement changed)\n    plus three more genuinely stagnant passes -- each still its own\n    exhausted ladder -- to trip the stagnation guard. The guard archives the\n    approach and routes to `replan` (v0.36 requirement F.1), ending in\n    `(\"advance\", \"replan\", \"stagnation_exhausted\")`; `_make_sup` configures\n    `max_approaches=1`, so that replan holds `exhausted`.","descriptionHtml":"<p>The scheduler assigns &quot;001&quot; (first in list order, no priority/deps).<br />\nThe fake agent's payload instead claims completion of &quot;002&quot; -- a task<br />\nit was never assigned. Task 116's ORIGINAL claim, pinned here before<br />\nv0.13 task 006 (#92 site 4)'s cutover, was: <code>outcome == (&quot;tail&quot;,)</code> and<br />\n<code>sup._abort_reason</code> mentioning &quot;contract violation&quot; -- a single<br />\ndisagreeing claim was fatal on the FIRST offence, with no re-ask and no<br />\nladder at all.</p>\n<pre><code>The NEW claim keeps the old one's real content -- the move is STILL\nrefused, and the record that actually persists is the harness's OWN\ndecision: &quot;001&quot; sits exactly where the harness itself put it\n(`in-progress`, claimed before spawn), &quot;002&quot; is untouched (still\n`pending`) -- and adds what the old assertion could not see: the\ndisagreement is carried back to the SAME worker verbatim on every\nre-ask through `contract_enforcement.enforce_contract` (the EXACT SAME\nladder `_step_generic_hat`'s sites 1/2 and worker's own site 3 already\nuse), the ladder runs the FULL `contract_retry_max + 1` attempts each\npass (never fewer, never more), and an exhausted ladder is an\nagent-fault continuation -- never an abort, no `_abort_reason`, no\n&quot;contract violation&quot; log message. Because the disagreement never\nresolves, tasks.json never moves on any pass, so it takes exactly one\npass to record every task's fresh `criteriaFingerprint` baseline (task\n008's own first-sight bookkeeping, itself &quot;progress&quot; for the\nstagnation counter even though nothing about the disagreement changed)\nplus three more genuinely stagnant passes -- each still its own\nexhausted ladder -- to trip the stagnation guard. The guard archives the\napproach and routes to `replan` (v0.36 requirement F.1), ending in\n`(&quot;advance&quot;, &quot;replan&quot;, &quot;stagnation_exhausted&quot;)`; `_make_sup` configures\n`max_approaches=1`, so that replan holds `exhausted`.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791980249814,"stop":1791980249814,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791980249815,"stop":1791980249815,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791980793260,"stop":1791980793260,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791980793261,"stop":1791980793277,"duration":16},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791980793277,"stop":1791980793278,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791980793278,"stop":179198079329